# el++ engine fixture 35 (src/test.slop: test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).
# Rule (17) from its triple premise: b is a B, so self(b, s) holds in G from
# the start. A's run (A reaches the nominal {b}, so it is unsafe and runs on
# its own) derives triple(x, r, b); that self fact is G's, never a fact of
# A's run, so only the triple's side can join r ∘ s ⊑ t: x t→ b, and with
# ∃t.B ⊑ D, A ⊑ D.
# Expect: A ⊑ D.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty . :t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:b a owl:NamedIndividual , :B .
:t owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :r :s ) .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:hasSelf true ] .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom [ owl:oneOf ( :b ) ] ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :t ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :D .
